  I've long been interested in mythology, and I got this big world
mythology book for Christmas.  I had the idea of looking up all the gods
of nethack in the index (except the discworld gods of course), and I
couldn't find any of the barbarian's gods or the rogue's gods and I only
found one of the archeologist's gods (Quetzacoutl of couse). (All the
other gods were in there except the neutral monk's god). Can someone
tell me where the barbarian's and rogue's gods are from?  (I had heard
of Crom before from the very little Irish mythology I am familiar with.)

The first section of the book is about Egypt, and after reading it, I
think the wizard's gods should be lawful-Osiris (God of order and the
underworld- even though he is god of the underworld, he seems to be the
most good god in Egypt. (instead of Ptah- the current lawful wizard god
who is a creator god who isn't much a part of the myths about other gods
-at least I got that impression from the book). neutral-Thoth (God of
wisdom), I agree with that one, except the goddess Isis might me a good
choice for wizards since she was the one most associated with magic
among the gods. chaotic- Seth (God of disorder who was long at war with
Osiris and Horus, the son of Osiris) seems the obvious choice. The book
didn't say very much about Anhur (one of several gods of war and the
current choice for nethack's chaotic wizard), so I got the (possibly
wrong) impression that he was a much less-important god.

I also think Hermes is a wrong choice for healers, since he isn't a
major god, nor is he much associated with healing. Although I don't
really think any greek god is much associated with healing, but maybe I
wouldn't know. (I haven't read that section yet, but I already know some
Greek mythology -Greek and Roman being the most popular of world
mythologies. I have read the Odyssey.)

..not that it matters that much, since nethack's gods are really all
exactly the same except in name and alignment.

